      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T10:12:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should guess the interface from the network here. The source of truth for Network -\u003e interfaces is the callback provided by MdnsSocketProvider; this should be used instead of post-guessing from the Network. Having 2 different paths guessing the association will lead to inconsistencies (for example, what if the interface doesn\u0027t have the multicast flag at this time, so it isn\u0027t actually being used for advertising ?)\n\nI think getting the interface from MdnsAdvertiser should be fairly easy if you make another version of onRegisterServiceSucceeded that is called for every registration on each interface (onRegisterServiceSucceededOnInterface ?), and has the interface as argument. You just need to relay the MdnsInterfaceAdvertiser.Callback.onRegisterServiceSucceeded call from MdnsAdvertiser.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1543,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 1543,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "637f5afb972e95e2009e0fca7e525ccdbdb98420",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
